<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort San Marcos de Apalache</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1679</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort San Marcos de Apalache was a Spanish fort at the junction of the Wakulla and St. Marks rivers in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, first built in 1679 to protect the Apalachee missions and their port. Rebuilt several times, it was held by the British from 1763 to 1783 and briefly captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-augustus-bowles">William Augustus Bowles</a> in 1800. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a> seized it in 1818 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-seminole-war">First Seminole War</a>, and its site is now a state park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-san-marcos-de-apalache.jpg" alt="Fort San Marcos de Apalache" width="300" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Noles1984 at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FLMap-doton-Fort-Ward.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
